{"id":"CVE-2017-3730","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"openssl","published":"2017-05-04T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T17:48:53.722Z","title":"Bad (EC)DHE parameters cause a client crash","description":"In OpenSSL 1.1.0 before 1.1.0d, if a malicious server supplies bad parameters for a DHE or ECDHE key exchange then this can result in the client attempting to dereference a NULL pointer leading to a client crash. This could be exploited in a Denial of Service attack.","cwe":["NULL pointer deference"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","other":"unknown","content":"{\"lang\": \"eng\", \"url\": \"https://www.openssl.org/policies/secpolicy.html#Moderate\", \"value\": \"Moderate\"}"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"OpenSSL","product":"OpenSSL","versions":["affected openssl-1.1.0","affected openssl-1.1.0a","affected openssl-1.1.0b","affected openssl-1.1.0c"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpujan2018-3236628.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/41192/","tags":["exploit","x_refsource_EXPLOIT-DB"],"name":"41192"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/95812","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"95812"},{"url":"https://github.com/openssl/openssl/commit/efbe126e3ebb9123ac9d058aa2bb044261342aaa","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.openssl.org/news/secadv/20170126.txt","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id/1037717","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1037717"},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpuoct2017-3236626.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201702-07","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-201702-07"},{"url":"https://support.hpe.com/hpsc/doc/public/display?docLocale=en_US&docId=emr_na-hpesbhf03838en_us","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpuapr2019-5072813.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"credits":["Guido Vranken"],"exploitdb":[{"edb":"41192","title":"OpenSSL 1.1.0 - Remote Client Denial of Service","type":"dos","platform":"multiple","date":"2017-01-26","verified":"0"}],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2017-3731","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"openssl","published":"2017-05-04T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T22:40:54.865Z","title":"Truncated packet could crash via OOB read","description":"If an SSL/TLS server or client is running on a 32-bit host, and a specific cipher is being used, then a truncated packet can cause that server or client to perform an out-of-bounds read, usually resulting in a crash. For OpenSSL 1.1.0, the crash can be triggered when using CHACHA20/POLY1305; users should upgrade to 1.1.0d. For Openssl 1.0.2, the crash can be triggered when using RC4-MD5; users who have not disabled that algorithm should update to 1.0.2k.","cwe":["out-of-bounds read"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","other":"unknown","content":"{\"lang\": \"eng\", \"url\": \"https://www.openssl.org/policies/secpolicy.html#Moderate\", \"value\": \"Moderate\"}"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"OpenSSL","product":"OpenSSL","versions":["affected openssl-1.1.0","affected openssl-1.1.0a","affected openssl-1.1.0b","affected openssl-1.1.0c","affected openssl-1.0.2","affected openssl-1.0.2a","affected openssl-1.0.2b","affected openssl-1.0.2c","affected openssl-1.0.2d","affected openssl-1.0.2e","affected openssl-1.0.2f","affected openssl-1.0.2g","affected openssl-1.0.2h","affected openssl-1.0.2i","affected openssl-1.0.2j"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:2185","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:2185"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:2186","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:2186"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20171019-0002/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpujan2018-3236628.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/95813","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"95813"},{"url":"http://rhn.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2017-0286.html","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2017:0286"},{"url":"https://security.FreeBSD.org/advisories/FreeBSD-SA-17:02.openssl.asc","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FREEBSD"],"name":"FreeBSD-SA-17:02"},{"url":"https://www.openssl.org/news/secadv/20170126.txt","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id/1037717","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1037717"},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpuoct2017-3236626.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://www.tenable.com/security/tns-2017-04","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://source.android.com/security/bulletin/pixel/2017-11-01","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201702-07","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-201702-07"},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpujul2017-3236622.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.debian.org/security/2017/dsa-3773","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-3773"},{"url":"https://support.hpe.com/hpsc/doc/public/display?docLocale=en_US&docId=emr_na-hpesbhf03838en_us","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:2187","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:2187"},{"url":"https://github.com/openssl/openssl/commit/00d965474b22b54e4275232bc71ee0c699c5cd21","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpuapr2019-5072813.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://security.paloaltonetworks.com/CVE-2017-3731","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"credits":["Robert Święcki of Google"],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2017-3732","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"openssl","published":"2017-05-04T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T22:08:37.371Z","title":"BN_mod_exp may produce incorrect results on x86_64","description":"There is a carry propagating bug in the x86_64 Montgomery squaring procedure in OpenSSL 1.0.2 before 1.0.2k and 1.1.0 before 1.1.0d. No EC algorithms are affected. Analysis suggests that attacks against RSA and DSA as a result of this defect would be very difficult to perform and are not believed likely. Attacks against DH are considered just feasible (although very difficult) because most of the work necessary to deduce information about a private key may be performed offline. The amount of resources required for such an attack would be very significant and likely only accessible to a limited number of attackers. An attacker would additionally need online access to an unpatched system using the target private key in a scenario with persistent DH parameters and a private key that is shared between multiple clients. For example this can occur by default in OpenSSL DHE based SSL/TLS ciphersuites. Note: This issue is very similar to CVE-2015-3193 but must be treated as a separate problem.","cwe":["carry-propagating bug"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","other":"unknown","content":"{\"lang\": \"eng\", \"url\": \"https://www.openssl.org/policies/secpolicy.html#Moderate\", \"value\": \"Moderate\"}"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"OpenSSL","product":"OpenSSL","versions":["affected openssl-1.1.0","affected openssl-1.1.0a","affected openssl-1.1.0b","affected openssl-1.1.0c","affected openssl-1.0.2","affected openssl-1.0.2a","affected openssl-1.0.2b","affected openssl-1.0.2c","affected openssl-1.0.2d","affected openssl-1.0.2e","affected openssl-1.0.2f","affected openssl-1.0.2g","affected openssl-1.0.2h","affected openssl-1.0.2i","affected openssl-1.0.2j"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:2185","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:2185"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:2186","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:2186"},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpujan2018-3236628.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:2713","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:2713"},{"url":"https://github.com/openssl/openssl/commit/a59b90bf491410f1f2bc4540cc21f1980fd14c5b","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://security.FreeBSD.org/advisories/FreeBSD-SA-17:02.openssl.asc","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FREEBSD"],"name":"FreeBSD-SA-17:02"},{"url":"https://www.openssl.org/news/secadv/20170126.txt","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id/1037717","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1037717"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:2575","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:2575"},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpuoct2017-3236626.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://www.tenable.com/security/tns-2017-04","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201702-07","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_GENTOO"],"name":"GLSA-201702-07"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:2568","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:2568"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/95814","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"95814"},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpujul2017-3236622.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://support.hpe.com/hpsc/doc/public/display?docLocale=en_US&docId=emr_na-hpesbhf03838en_us","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:2187","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:2187"},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpuapr2019-5072813.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"credits":["OSS-Fuzz project"],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2017-3733","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"openssl","published":"2017-05-04T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T16:18:03.381Z","title":"Encrypt-Then-Mac renegotiation crash","description":"During a renegotiation handshake if the Encrypt-Then-Mac extension is negotiated where it was not in the original handshake (or vice-versa) then this can cause OpenSSL 1.1.0 before 1.1.0e to crash (dependent on ciphersuite). Both clients and servers are affected.","cwe":["protocol error"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","other":"unknown","content":"{\"lang\": \"eng\", \"url\": \"https://www.openssl.org/policies/secpolicy.html#High\", \"value\": \"High\"}"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"OpenSSL","product":"OpenSSL","versions":["affected openssl-1.1.0","affected openssl-1.1.0a","affected openssl-1.1.0b","affected openssl-1.1.0c","affected openssl-1.1.0d"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/96269","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"96269"},{"url":"https://www.openssl.org/news/secadv/20170216.txt","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpujan2018-3236628.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://h20566.www2.hpe.com/hpsc/doc/public/display?docLocale=en_US&docId=emr_na-hpesbgn03728en_us","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpuoct2017-3236626.html","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://github.com/openssl/openssl/commit/4ad93618d26a3ea23d36ad5498ff4f59eff3a4d2","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id/1037846","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1037846"},{"url":"https://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpuapr2019-5072813.html","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]}],"credits":["Joe Orton (Red Hat)"],"vendors":["openssl"]}
{"id":"CVE-2017-3735","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"openssl","published":"2017-08-28T19:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T21:08:28.987Z","description":"While parsing an IPAddressFamily extension in an X.509 certificate, it is possible to do a one-byte overread. This would result in an incorrect text display of the certificate. This bug has been present since 2006 and is present in all versions of OpenSSL before 1.0.2m and 1.1.0g.","cwe":["out of bounds read"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"OpenSSL Software Foundation","product":"OpenSSL","versions":["affected 1.1.0","affected 1.0.2"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id/1039726","tags":["vdb-entry"],"name":"1039726"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3611-2/","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"USN-3611-2"},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2017/dsa-4018","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"DSA-4018"},{"url":"https://security.gentoo.org/glsa/201712-03","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"GLSA-201712-03"},{"url":"https://lists.debian.org/debian-lts-announce/2017/11/msg00011.html","tags":["mailing-list"],"name":"[debian-lts-announce] 20171109 [SECURITY] [DLA-1157-1] openssl security update"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:3505","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"RHSA-2018:3505"},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2017/dsa-4017","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"DSA-4017"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:3221","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"RHSA-2018:3221"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/100515","tags":["vdb-entry"],"name":"100515"},{"url":"https://security.FreeBSD.org/advisories/FreeBSD-SA-17:11.openssl.asc","tags":["vendor-advisory"],"name":"FreeBSD-SA-17:11"},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpujul2018-4258247.html"},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpujan2018-3236628.html"},{"url":"http://www.oracle.com/technetwork/security-advisory/cpuapr2018-3678067.html"},{"url":"http://www